From 58d4342ab0c5f5239108d30efa5ad2990879e037 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Riley <oreo4455@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:50:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: Disconnect requestCompleted on close

The source connects to the camera's requestCompleted signal on every open
and never disconnects. When the camera manager (and so the camera) outlives
a close, reopening adds a second connection: each request completes twice,
the second call pops the next RequestWrap (assertion
'wrap->request_.get() == request'), and the pipeline crashes on a freed
request. Disconnect when the camera is released.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp b/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
index 3055f0d..c101976 100644
--- a/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
+++ b/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
@@ -1001,6 +1001,13 @@ gst_libcamera_src_close(GstLibcameraSrc *self)
 
 	state->config_.reset();
 
+	/*
+	 * Connected on every open: the camera outlives a close whenever the
+	 * camera manager does, and a second connection completes each request
+	 * twice (the second pops the wrong RequestWrap, then a use after free).
+	 */
+	state->cam_->requestCompleted.disconnect(state);
+
 	ret = state->cam_->release();
 	if (ret) {
 		GST_ELEMENT_WARNING(self, RESOURCE, BUSY,
-- 
